// shader-differential — control-discard side A (CF-2 acceptance, 2026-09-02).
//
// Kills the 16 left-hand columns (TEXCOORD0.x = u < 0.25 at the pixel
// centres) and paints the rest with a ramp.  The stager GENERATES side B
// from this source with the band widened to u < 0.5 (32 columns), and
// both sides are REFERENCE-compiled: the row measures the judge, not the
// compiler.  What the guest asserts: mismatch, painted a=3072 b=2048,
// exactly 1024 differing pixels (the columns A paints and B kills), and a
// KIL decoded in both containers.  A judge that could not see a wrong
// discard as a wrong band fails the run here, before any discard witness
// (th06, discard-blend, test_57_discard, fp_discard_then_work_f) is read.
//
// The companion control-discard-blind row is one generated program whose
// KIL cannot fire (v.x < -1 on a 0..1 lane) byte-copied to both sides; it
// must judge discard-blind, proving the instrument that names a witness
// whose discard never ran under the rig's inputs.
void main(float4 v : TEXCOORD0, out float4 color : COLOR)
{
    if (v.x < 0.25f) discard;
    color = float4(v.x, v.y, 0.5f, 1.0f);
}
